<title>POLAND: Polish passenger car sales rise 34 pct in Jan-Feb.</title>
<headline>Polish passenger car sales rise 34 pct in Jan-Feb.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>New passenger car sales in Poland in the first two months of the year rose by 33.96 percent against the same period last year to 85,152 units, data collected by the Samar car market monitoring company showed.</p>
<p>Sales of commercial vehicles in that period rose 39.5 percent to 8,450 untis, Samar said.</p>
<p>Passenger car sales were lead by Fiat with 29,077 units sold, giving the Italian company a 34.2 percent market share.</p>
<p>South Korea's Daewoo was the first in commercial vehicles sales with 4,500 units and a 53.4 percent market share.</p>
